  CLAUSE 1 -- BOOKKEEPING, PER EIGHTH. A pinned index makes the cells
  DIAGONAL, so T1.ORACLE's residual is identically zero and its slot term
  IS its gap. Arithmetic, not a result -- and a windowed scorer has to earn
  it again in every eighth. `ident` is gap - (slot + residual), worst case.
    ORACLE residual, worst eighth        0.00e+00   over 0 creature-eighths   *** FAIL -- EMPTY SET ***
    identity, worst creature x eighth    0.00e+00   PASS
    and over EVERY arm and eighth        0.00e+00   over 0 creature-eighths   *** FAIL -- EMPTY SET ***

  CLAUSE 2 -- VACUITY, at the PRIMARY'S GRANULARITY and on the arm that is
  KNOWN to express. The question a vacuity gate must answer here is whether
  a ~17-probe window can carry a large slot term AT ALL, and only an arm
  that expresses can answer it -- the derived arm's own column could not
  (`vacuity-gate-cannot-guard-a-rejection`). Required: >= 0.08 in >= 6 of 8.
